{
  "heading": "pagerts - Webpage URL extractor",
  "content": [
    "pagerts is a secure, modern TypeScript CLI tool that transforms URLs into structured JSON objects, extracting all navigable items and resources from webpages.",
    {
      "heading": "Features",
      "content": [
        "🔒 **Security-First** - Built-in URL validation, rate limiting, and XSS protection",
        "🚀 **Modern TypeScript** - Strict type checking and modern ES2022 syntax",
        "⚡ **Fast** - Efficient parsing with LinkeDOM and concurrent request handling",
        "🧪 **Well-Tested** - Comprehensive test coverage with Jest",
        "📦 **Easy to Use** - Simple CLI interface with sensible defaults",
        "🗂️ **Local File Support** - Parses local file paths and file:/// inputs",
        "🧭 **Request Header Override** - Optional --user-agent flag for sites that behave differently by client"
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Installation",
      "content": [
        {
          "heading": "Global Installation",
          "content": [
            "npm install -g pagerts",
            "",
            "pagerts ./page.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Using npx (No Installation Required)",
          "content": "npx pagerts ./page.html"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Usage",
      "content": [
        {
          "heading": "Extract from local HTML file",
          "content": "pagerts ./page.html"
        },
        {
          "heading": "Extract from local file URL",
          "content": "pagerts file:///path/to/file.html"
        },
        {
          "heading": "Fetch from remote URL",
          "content": "pagerts fetch https://website.com"
        },
        {
          "heading": "Override user-agent",
          "content": "pagerts fetch --user-agent 'Mozilla/5.0...' https://example.com"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Output",
      "content": [
        "The output is JSON containing:",
        {
          "heading": "title",
          "content": "Page's title from <title> tag"
        },
        {
          "heading": "url",
          "content": "URL of the page"
        },
        {
          "heading": "resources",
          "content": "Array of resources (links, meta tags, embeds) with name and url fields"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Links",
